---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import { company, site, power, network, compute } from '../data/site';
---
<Content
  title={`RTX and B300 compute in Mead, Oklahoma | ${company.full}`}
  description={`The initial SmartTec deployment includes ${compute.phaseSystems} at ${site.designation}. Explore the planned hardware, workload review and commissioning schedule.`}
  kicker="The first compute deployment"
  heading="Two platforms. One starting point."
  lede={`The initial plan combines two RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell nodes with one B300 node at ${site.name}. We are matching the hardware, cooling and software to customer workloads as the campus moves through fit-out and commissioning.`}
  meta={[
    { label: 'Initial deployment', value: String(compute.servers + compute.b300Servers) + ' nodes', note: compute.phaseSystems, tone: 'signal' },
    { label: 'RTX GPUs', value: String(compute.gpus), note: 'Four per RTX node', count: true },
    { label: 'RTX memory', value: compute.vramPerGpu, note: 'Per GPU, separate memories' },
    { label: 'Deployment status', value: 'Planned', note: 'Procurement and commissioning not complete', tone: 'gold' },
  ]}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="fleet" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">01</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Initial hardware</span></p>
    <h2 id="fleet">RTX nodes and B300 are both in the first phase.</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card__tag mono-label">{compute.servers} planned nodes</p>
        <h3>RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell</h3>
        <p>Each node is planned with {compute.gpusPerServer} {compute.gpuModel} GPUs, each with {compute.vramPerGpu} of memory. The two nodes provide {compute.gpus} RTX GPUs in total.</p>
        <p>{compute.workloads}. Large models and training workloads are assessed against the selected configuration.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card__tag mono-label">{compute.b300Servers} planned node</p>
        <h3>B300</h3>
        <p>A B300 node is included in the initial deployment alongside the RTX nodes. Its final server configuration and workload allocation will be specified in the deployment proposal.</p>
        <p>The RTX GPU count, memory figures and load estimate on this page apply only to the two RTX nodes.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="callout" style="margin-top: var(--s-6);">
      <p><strong>Development status.</strong> The fleet is planned and has not completed procurement and commissioning. Customer availability depends on equipment acceptance and the readiness of the facility and network.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="configuration" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">02</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Match the workload</span></p>
    <h2 id="configuration">Choose capacity around the job.</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>Tell us the application, model size, memory needs, storage throughput and intended software stack. We use those requirements to assess the appropriate platform and dedicated allocation.</p>
        <p>The RTX GPUs each have separate {compute.vramPerGpu} memories. Applications that span GPUs need a suitable parallel execution strategy; the eight cards do not form one pooled memory space.</p>
        <p>For an existing workload, representative benchmarks help establish fit before a commercial commitment.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="spec">
        <div><dt>RTX configuration</dt><dd>{compute.servers} nodes × {compute.gpusPerServer} GPUs<span class="note">{compute.gpuModel}</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>RTX memory</dt><dd>{compute.vramPerGpu} per GPU<span class="note">Separate memories; no NVLink on this part.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>RTX IT load estimate</dt><dd>{compute.load}<span class="note">Two RTX nodes only. Excludes the B300 node and facility cooling; not a measured load.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>B300 deployment</dt><dd>{compute.b300Servers} planned node<span class="note">Configuration and load established with the selected system.</span></dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/model-planner">Explore model requirements</a></div>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="cooling" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">03</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Campus integration</span></p>
    <h2 id="cooling">Designed with the power and thermal system.</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>The proposed cooling architecture uses a warm-water loop for compatible liquid-cooled servers and a separate chilled-water loop for active rear-door heat exchangers. Both use closed circuits and dry heat rejection. Equipment selection and mechanical review establish the final configuration.</p>
        <p>The campus electrical commissioning milestone is an {power.commissioningTarget}. Planned {network.provider} fiber has an {network.deliveryTarget}. These are management targets, with customer service following facility, equipment and network acceptance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Explore the infrastructure</h3>
        <p>See the two-loop thermal diagram, shared electrical service and the phased campus plan.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a href="/power#thermal">Power and cooling →</a><a href="/site">Campus plan →</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="is-end" aria-labelledby="buying" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">04</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Start a conversation</span></p>
    <h2 id="buying">Bring us your workload.</h2>
    <p>We review platform fit, capacity, timing and support needs, then provide a proposal with the selected configuration and commercial terms. You can also discuss colocation for hardware you already own.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Discuss compute requirements</a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/colocation">Explore colocation</a></div>
  </section>
</Content>
